Helm in Multi-Cluster Environments
Lab Objectives
By the end of this lab, you will be able to:

Set up and configure Helm for managing multiple Kubernetes clusters
Create and manage multiple Kubernetes clusters on a single machine using kind
Deploy applications across multiple clusters using Helm
Understand multi-cluster deployment strategies and best practices
Manage Helm releases across different cluster contexts
Implement cross-cluster application deployment workflows
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, you should have:

Basic understanding of Kubernetes concepts (pods, services, deployments)
Familiarity with YAML configuration files
Basic command-line interface experience
Understanding of containerization concepts
Previous experience with Helm basics (charts, releases, repositories)
