Troubleshooting Common Issues
Issue 1: Cluster Creation Failures
If kind cluster creation fails:

# Check Docker status
sudo systemctl status docker

# Restart Docker if needed
sudo systemctl restart docker

# Clean up failed clusters
kind delete clusters --all

# Recreate clusters
kind create cluster --config=dev-cluster-config.yaml
Issue 2: Helm Deployment Failures
If Helm deployments fail:

# Check Helm status
helm status <release-name> -n <namespace>

# Debug deployment issues
kubectl describe deployment <deployment-name> -n <namespace>

# Check pod logs
kubectl logs -l app.kubernetes.io/name=multi-cluster-app -n <namespace>
Issue 3: Context Switching Issues
If kubectl context switching fails:

# List available contexts
kubectl config get-contexts

# Manually set context
kubectl config use-context <context-name>

# Verify current context
kubectl config current-context
Best Practices for Multi-Cluster Helm Management
1. Environment Separation
Use different values files for each environment
Implement proper resource limits and requests
Use environment-specific configurations
2. Deployment Strategy
Deploy to development first, then staging, then production
Implement proper testing between deployments
Use automated rollback mechanisms
3. Security Considerations
Use different secrets for each environment
Implement proper RBAC policies
Secure inter-cluster communications
4. Monitoring and Observability
Implement centralized logging
Monitor resource usage across clusters
Set up alerting for deployment failures
